            "sourceShape": "http://iec.ch/TC57/ns/CIM/CoreEquipment-EU/Constraints#TapChangerTablePoint.r-datatype",
            "schemaDescription": "The resistance deviation as a percentage of nominal value. The actual reactance is calculated as follows:\ncalculated resistance = r(nominal) * (1 + r(from this class)/100).   The r(nominal) is defined as the static resistance on the associated power transformer end or ends.  This model assumes the star impedance (pi model) form.",
            "schemaMultiplicity": "0..1",
            "classDescription": "Describes each tap step in the ratio tap changer tabular curve."
          }
        },
