          "properties": {
            "count": 1,
            "key": "IdentifiedObject.name",
            "sampleIDs": [
              "08464663-7dbf-4195-9754-a6ff63c421d6"
            ],
            "violationType": "sh:minCount",
            "sourceShape": "http://iec.ch/TC57/ns/CIM/IdentifiedObject/constraints/3.0#IdentifiedObject.name-cardinality",
            "schemaDescription": "The name is any free human readable and possibly non unique text naming the object.",
            "schemaMultiplicity": "1..1",
            "classDescription": "A wire or combination of wires, with consistent electrical characteristics, building a single electrical system, used to carry alternating current between points in the power system.\nFor symmetrical, transposed three phase lines, it is sufficient to use attributes of the line segment, which describe impedances and admittances for the entire length of the segment.  Additionally impedances can be computed by using length and associated per length impedances.\nThe BaseVoltage at the two ends of ACLineSegments in a Line shall have the same BaseVoltage.nominalVoltage. However, boundary lines may have slightly different BaseVoltage.nominalVoltages and variation is allowed. Larger voltage difference in general requires use of an equivalent branch."
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "PowerTransformerEnd-terminalConsistency/sh:sparql",
          "ruleIndex": 34,
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "The Terminal referenced by TransformerEnd.Terminal points to a PowerTransformer which is different than the referenced element via PowerTransformerEnd.PowerTransformer. \u2014 1 object(s) affected. Examples: PowerTransformerEnd 97dad686-69db-a271-59c1-2ab23e543ab1 (STUPET_G2_TRAFO)"
          },
          "occurrenceCount": 1,
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "PowerTransformerEnd/97dad686-69db-a271-59c1-2ab23e543ab1",
                  "name": "STUPET_G2_TRAFO",
                  "kind": "object"
                }
              ],
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "Instance/Svedala/Grid/cimxml/20220615T2230Z__Svedala_EQ_1.xml"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 26011
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "count": 1,
            "key": "type",
            "sampleIDs": [
              "97dad686-69db-a271-59c1-2ab23e543ab1"
            ],
            "violationType": "sh:sparql",
            "sourceShape": "http://iec.ch/TC57/ns/CIM/Equipment-EU/constraints/IEC61970-301/3.0#PowerTransformerEnd-terminalConsistency",
            "schemaDescription": "The nature or genre of the resource. Recommended practice is to use a controlled vocabulary such as the DCMI Type Vocabulary [DCMI-TYPE]. To describe the file format, physical medium, or dimensions of the resource, use the property Format.",
            "schemaMultiplicity": "0..1",
            "classDescription": "A PowerTransformerEnd is associated with each Terminal of a PowerTransformer.\nThe impedance values r, r0, x, and x0 of a PowerTransformerEnd represents a star equivalent as follows.\n1) for a two Terminal PowerTransformer the high voltage (TransformerEnd.endNumber=1) PowerTransformerEnd has non zero values on r, r0, x, and x0 while the low voltage (TransformerEnd.endNumber=2) PowerTransformerEnd has zero values for r, r0, x, and x0.  Parameters are always provided, even if the PowerTransformerEnds have the same rated voltage.  In this case, the parameters are provided at the PowerTransformerEnd which has TransformerEnd.endNumber equal to 1.\n2) for a three Terminal PowerTransformer the three PowerTransformerEnds represent a star equivalent with each leg in the star represented by r, r0, x, and x0 values.\n3) For a three Terminal transformer each PowerTransformerEnd shall have g, g0, b and b0 values corresponding to the no load losses distributed on the three PowerTransformerEnds. The total no load loss shunt impedances may also be placed at one of the PowerTransformerEnds, preferably the end numbered 1, having the shunt values on end 1.  This is the preferred way.\n4) for a PowerTransformer with more than three Terminals the PowerTransformerEnd impedance values cannot be used. Instead use the TransformerMeshImpedance or split the transformer into multiple PowerTransformers.\nEach PowerTransformerEnd must be contained by a PowerTransformer. Because a PowerTransformerEnd (or any other object) can not be contained by more than one parent, a PowerTransformerEnd can not have an association to an EquipmentContainer (Substation, VoltageLevel, etc)."
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "PowerTransformerEnd.ratedU-valueRange/sh:sparql",
          "ruleIndex": 35,
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "The PowerTransformerEnd.ratedU does not fuifil one of the following: 1) it is not a positive value; 2) the value of the high voltage side shall be greater than or equal to ratedU for the lower voltage sides. \u2014 1 object(s) affected. Examples: PowerTransformer 555aceb5-a63e-4acb-a820-be850f080160 (NORRSELE_G1_TRAFO)"
          },
          "occurrenceCount": 1,
          "locations": [
